From: KOReader <https://github.com/koreader/koreader-base>
Subject: [PATCH] fitz/unlibarchive: fix the Windows include paths

`#ifdef _WIN32` pulls in `libarchive/archive.h` / `libarchive/archive_entry.h`,
which matches neither the MSVC/vcpkg layout nor MinGW's: libarchive installs
its headers flat (`<archive.h>`, `<archive_entry.h>`).

This is yet another Windows-only path upstream never built, so it only shows
up when actually compiling for Windows. Use the same includes as everywhere
else.

--- a/source/fitz/unlibarchive.c
+++ b/source/fitz/unlibarchive.c
@@ -24,13 +24,8 @@
 
 #ifdef HAVE_LIBARCHIVE
 
-#ifdef _WIN32
-#include "libarchive/archive.h"
-#include "libarchive/archive_entry.h"
-#else
 #include <archive.h>
 #include <archive_entry.h>
-#endif
 
 typedef struct
 {
